export default {"format":"cadcraft-help","version":1,"app":"bimcraft","addon":"pointcloud","name":"Point clouds","sections":{"start":"Getting started","tasks":"Walkthroughs","switching":"Coming from other software","reference":"Reference","trouble":"Troubleshooting and limits"},"topics":[{"slug":"point-clouds-here","scope":"addon:pointcloud","title":"Point clouds in BimCraft and CadCraft","summary":"With the Point clouds add-on, open a LAS, LAZ, E57, PLY, OBJ, USDZ, PCD, PTX, XYZ or PTS cloud or phone scan of millions of points, see all of it in the app's 3D view, clean it with a lasso or box, and cut a section through it.","section":"tasks","order":63,"keywords":["point cloud","phone scan","iphone","ipad","lidar scan","obj","usdz","compare with model","deviation","tolerance","as-built","field-verified","las","laz","e57","ply","pcd","ptx","xyz","pts","scan","lidar","clean","lasso","noise","classify","ground","section","3d","add-on","tiles"],"headings":[{"id":"open-a-cloud","text":"Open a cloud","level":2},{"id":"phone-scans","text":"Phone scans","level":2},{"id":"compare-with-model-bimcraft","text":"Compare with model (BimCraft)","level":2},{"id":"where-it-sits","text":"Where it sits","level":2},{"id":"clean-it","text":"Clean it","level":2},{"id":"sort-it-bimcraft-only","text":"Sort it (BimCraft only)","level":2},{"id":"section-strip","text":"Section strip","level":2},{"id":"not-built-yet","text":"Not built yet","level":2}],"html":"\u003Cp\u003EMost people never need this, so it is an add-on. Switch on \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EPoint clouds\u003C/span\u003E in Settings › Add-ons; a \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EPoint clouds\u003C/span\u003E tab (BimCraft) or section (CadCraft) appears in the right-hand panel. The file is read in your browser and the tiles are kept in this browser&#039;s own storage, or in a folder you pick; nothing is uploaded.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Caside class=\"hc hc-warning\"\u003E\u003Cp class=\"hc-label\"\u003EWarning\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EEverything this tab reports is a number from your data, not a certificate. It was tested on a made-up site and on small made-up files in each app, not on a real scan: read the first results with care and tell us what you find.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/aside\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EIt is the same add-on as in CivilCraft, with the same engine; only the part that draws in the app&#039;s own 3D view differs. The app&#039;s older Attach / Place / Register scan tools are separate and unchanged.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"open-a-cloud\"\u003EOpen a cloud\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EOpen a model first in BimCraft (the 3D view is made with the first model), or the 3D tab in CadCraft. Under \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EOpen a cloud\u003C/span\u003E choose a file. LAS and LAZ are tiled as they are, a piece at a time (a LAZ file is never copied whole into memory). E57 is read page by page and every point kept. PCD, PTX, XYZ and PTS are read by the app&#039;s own reader first, at most 3 million points kept (thinned evenly, the tab says so), then tiled the same way. Metres are assumed unless the file says feet. Press \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EBuild the cloud\u003C/span\u003E; a build can be stopped and resumed (LAS and LAZ). A big cloud is tiled by several workers at once.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"phone-scans\"\u003EPhone scans\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EScanning apps on an iPhone or iPad with a LiDAR sensor export a surface (a mesh), not a cloud of points. \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EOpen a cloud\u003C/span\u003E reads a PLY with faces, an OBJ, and a USDZ that holds an OBJ, a PLY or readable USDA text, lays points on the surface about every 10 mm (at most 3 million), keeps the colours, and checks the way the scan stands: if its layers say Y is up (the usual phone and game convention) it is turned Z up and its floor is levelled, and the tab says so. If it only seems that another axis is up, it is left alone and the tab tells you. A USDZ that holds only a binary USD file (a .usdc) is not read yet: export OBJ or PLY from the app.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Caside class=\"hc hc-warning\"\u003E\u003Cp class=\"hc-label\"\u003EWarning\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe readers follow the formats&#039; own documentation and were tested on files we wrote in those formats. A real export from a phone app was not available to test with: if yours fails, tell us which app and version made it.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003C/aside\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"compare-with-model-bimcraft\"\u003ECompare with model (BimCraft)\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWith a model and a cloud open, \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ECompare with model\u003C/span\u003E measures how far every scan point is from the nearest surface of the model&#039;s elements, draws the points coloured by that distance, and lists each element as within your tolerance (default 20 mm), outside it, only partly scanned (the points touch too small a part of it to say) or not scanned. \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ECheck scale and level\u003C/span\u003E first says whether the scan looks like another unit, has another axis up or has a floor that leans. The elements within tolerance can be marked field-verified in one step (method: scan, the tolerance in the note), and \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EDownload the report\u003C/span\u003E saves every element with its numbers as CSV.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EIt compares the scan with the model as placed in the 3D view. It is not a survey, and a scan that is shifted or at the wrong scale looks wrong everywhere.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"where-it-sits\"\u003EWhere it sits\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe cloud is drawn in the 3D view with coarse tiles that refine as you move closer, never more than \u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EMost points drawn\u003C/span\u003E at once. If the cloud&#039;s own coordinates overlap the model (or drawing), it is drawn where its numbers say, so a registered scan lines up with the design; otherwise it is centred on the model or drawing with its lowest point on the ground. Eye-dome lighting starts off in these apps: tick it to try.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"clean-it\"\u003EClean it\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EClean\u003C/span\u003E takes a lasso, a box or a polygon drawn over the 3D view (a vertical prism down to the cloud&#039;s middle height: use the Top view when it has to be exact), changes the class of the points inside, deletes them, restores them or crops to them. A noise filter finds stray points. Every step is one undo.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"sort-it-bimcraft-only\"\u003ESort it (BimCraft only)\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003EClassify\u003C/span\u003E finds the ground and then the geometric classes (low, medium and high vegetation, buildings), tile by tile. CadCraft does not have it: it carries no TIN or ground modules, and an add-on may not reach into another folder.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"section-strip\"\u003ESection strip\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan class=\"hui\"\u003ESection strip\u003C/span\u003E draws a line across the cloud and shows the points within a width of it, seen from the side.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 id=\"not-built-yet\"\u003ENot built yet\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EBuilding the ground into the model, contours, stockpile and flight-to-flight volumes, the orthomosaic drape and the plan raster are CivilCraft&#039;s; they are not in these two apps.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ECadCraft has no Classify.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA very large PCD, PTX, XYZ or PTS is read whole before tiling and keeps only 3 million points.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA binary USDZ (.usdc) is not read; GLB and glTF from scanning apps are not read yet.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA LAZ with variable chunks or the layered point formats (6 to 10) is read the older way, whole into memory.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ECompare with model is BimCraft&#039;s; CadCraft has no model of triangles to compare with.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENo change of coordinate system: metres assumed.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E","text":"Most people never need this, so it is an add-on. Switch on Point clouds in Settings › Add-ons; a Point clouds tab (BimCraft) or section (CadCraft) appears in the right-hand panel. The file is read in your browser and the tiles are kept in this browser's own storage, or in a folder you pick; nothing is uploaded. Everything this tab reports is a number from your data, not a certificate. It was tested on a made-up site and on small made-up files in each app, not on a real scan: read the first results with care and tell us what you find. It is the same add-on as in CivilCraft, with the same engine; only the part that draws in the app's own 3D view differs. The app's older Attach / Place / Register scan tools are separate and unchanged. Open a cloud Open a model first in BimCraft (the 3D view is made with the first model), or the 3D tab in CadCraft. Under Open a cloud choose a file. LAS and LAZ are tiled as they are, a piece at a time (a LAZ file is never copied whole into memory). E57 is read page by page and every point kept. PCD, PTX, XYZ and PTS are read by the app's own reader first, at most 3 million points kept (thinned evenly, the tab says so), then tiled the same way. Metres are assumed unless the file says feet. Press Build the cloud; a build can be stopped and resumed (LAS and LAZ). A big cloud is tiled by several workers at once. Phone scans Scanning apps on an iPhone or iPad with a LiDAR sensor export a surface (a mesh), not a cloud of points. Open a cloud reads a PLY with faces, an OBJ, and a USDZ that holds an OBJ, a PLY or readable USDA text, lays points on the surface about every 10 mm (at most 3 million), keeps the colours, and checks the way the scan stands: if its layers say Y is up (the usual phone and game convention) it is turned Z up and its floor is levelled, and the tab says so. If it only seems that another axis is up, it is left alone and the tab tells you. A USDZ that holds only a binary USD file (a .usdc) is not read yet: export OBJ or PLY from the app. The readers follow the formats' own documentation and were tested on files we wrote in those formats. A real export from a phone app was not available to test with: if yours fails, tell us which app and version made it. Compare with model (BimCraft) With a model and a cloud open, Compare with model measures how far every scan point is from the nearest surface of the model's elements, draws the points coloured by that distance, and lists each element as within your tolerance (default 20 mm), outside it, only partly scanned (the points touch too small a part of it to say) or not scanned. Check scale and level first says whether the scan looks like another unit, has another axis up or has a floor that leans. The elements within tolerance can be marked field-verified in one step (method: scan, the tolerance in the note), and Download the report saves every element with its numbers as CSV. It compares the scan with the model as placed in the 3D view. It is not a survey, and a scan that is shifted or at the wrong scale looks wrong everywhere. Where it sits The cloud is drawn in the 3D view with coarse tiles that refine as you move closer, never more than Most points drawn at once. If the cloud's own coordinates overlap the model (or drawing), it is drawn where its numbers say, so a registered scan lines up with the design; otherwise it is centred on the model or drawing with its lowest point on the ground. Eye-dome lighting starts off in these apps: tick it to try. Clean it Clean takes a lasso, a box or a polygon drawn over the 3D view (a vertical prism down to the cloud's middle height: use the Top view when it has to be exact), changes the class of the points inside, deletes them, restores them or crops to them. A noise filter finds stray points. Every step is one undo. Sort it (BimCraft only) Classify finds the ground and then the geometric classes (low, medium and high vegetation, buildings), tile by tile. CadCraft does not have it: it carries no TIN or ground modules, and an add-on may not reach into another folder. Section strip Section strip draws a line across the cloud and shows the points within a width of it, seen from the side. Not built yet Building the ground into the model, contours, stockpile and flight-to-flight volumes, the orthomosaic drape and the plan raster are CivilCraft's; they are not in these two apps. CadCraft has no Classify. A very large PCD, PTX, XYZ or PTS is read whole before tiling and keeps only 3 million points. A binary USDZ (.usdc) is not read; GLB and glTF from scanning apps are not read yet. A LAZ with variable chunks or the layered point formats (6 to 10) is read the older way, whole into memory. Compare with model is BimCraft's; CadCraft has no model of triangles to compare with. No change of coordinate system: metres assumed."}]};
